.TH MAN 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
man \- show a manual page
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B man
.RI [ section ]
.I name
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B man
finds the manual page for
.IR name ,
formats it for the terminal and shows it through a pager. Pages are
man(7) source, as on Linux, kept as
.IR /usr/share/man/man section / name . section .
With no
.IR section ,
sections 1, 8, 5 and 7 are searched, in that order.
.PP
On a terminal, the page is laid out to the terminal's width, with bold
and italic text (italics show underlined), and piped to
.B $MANPAGER
or
.BR $PAGER ,
else
.BR less (1).
Into a pipe or a file, the plain text is written, 80 columns wide.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MANPATH
The manual trees to search, separated by
.BR : ;
.I /usr/share/man
by default.
.TP
.B "MANPAGER PAGER"
The pager, run with
.BR "sh \-c" ;
the first set is used.
.TP
.B LESS
Left as it is; when it isn't set,
.B man
runs its pager with
.B LESS=\-R
(as man\-db does), so
.BR less (1)
shows bold and underline instead of their escape sequences.
.SH PAGE FORMAT
The formatter understands this part of man(7), and ignores other
requests:
.TP
.BI .TH " title section"
The page's title, shown in its header and footer.
.TP
.B ".SH .SS"
A section heading, a subsection heading.
.TP
.B ".PP .P .LP"
A new paragraph (so does a blank line).
.TP
.B .TP
A tagged paragraph: the next line is the tag, the lines after it the
indented body.
.TP
.BI .IP " tag"
A tagged paragraph with the tag given.
.TP
.B ".RS .RE"
Indent further, and back.
.TP
.B ".B .I"
The line in bold, in italics.
.TP
.B ".BR .RB .BI .IB .IR .RI"
Words in fonts taking turns, with no spaces between them (quote a word to
keep spaces in it).
.TP
.B ".nf .fi"
Lines as they are (no filling), and filled again.
.TP
.B ".br .sp"
A line break, a blank line.
.TP
.B .\e"
A comment.
.PP
In text:
.B \efB \efI \efR \efP
change the font (bold, italic, roman, the previous one);
.B \e\-
is a minus,
.B \ee
and
.B \e\e
a backslash,
.B \e(em
a dash, and
.B \e&
nothing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 with no name given; 16 if no page was found.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
man ls
man 1 sh
man less > less.txt
.fi
.SH NOTES
There are no options and no
.BR \-k ;
tables, other macros and other escapes are not supported.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR less (1)
